">4.35, 15.79</td><td align="left">14% (53%)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">GABRB1 (Chr 4: 51.4 cM)</td><td align="center">0.35</td><td align="center">4.81</td><td align="left">Sex, Age at onset</td><td align="left">Both male; both early age at onset</td><td align="left">0.20, 0.94</td><td align="left">19% (59%)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">D6S495 (Chr 6: 153.8 cM)</td><td align="center">1.19</td><td align="center">3.85</td><td align="left">Smokers, Max drinks</td><td align="left">One smokes, one not; one heavy drinker, one not</td><td align="left">8.00, 5.40</td><td align="left">19% (47%)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">D14s51 (Chr 14: 111.0 cM)</td><td align="center">0.043</td><td align="center">3.14</td><td align="left">Max drinks, Sex</td><td align="left">One heavy drinker, one not</td><td align="left">0.38, 0.01</td><td align="left">35% (52%)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">D20S50 (Chr 20: 13.6 cM)</td><td align="center">0.003</td><td align="center">3.20</td><td align="left">Sex, Smoking</td><td align="left">Both male; both smoker or both not smokers</td><td align="left">0.29, 0.07</td><td align="left">25%(54%)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>a</sup>Proportion of bootstrap trees that selected the same covariates (proportion that selected the same covariate at the first split).</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>